body:
Hey guys I am really sorry, but my VS 2015 holepessly fails to run any xUnit tests and I do not know how I should change that.

First of all, I am using Resharper to run the tests, as the xUnit VS Testrunner extension fails to install with a "object not set to an instance of an object" error. (another reason why I prefer NUnit - it just works, but everyone has its favorites and I want to use your frameworks)

However, when I run the tests, 800 of them are ignored by the Resharper Testrunner with the message

![image](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/1175751/11613575/385b7156-9c26-11e5-97da-8fdcb44bf4a6.png)

Now I wanted to solve that problem by just adding xunit as a nuget reference, however I saw that you actually copied the "FactAttribute" of xunit in XUnitConventions.cs

<pre>
namespace Xunit
{
    using System;
    [AttributeUsage(AttributeTargets.Method)]
    public class FactAttribute : Attribute {
        public string Skip { get; set; }
    }
    public interface IUseFixture<T> where T : new()
    {
        void SetFixture(T data);
    }
}
</pre>

 So you may have a reason to do this and I would like to know, what it is, and moreover, how I can get those testcases to work.

Otherwise I cannot proceed. Sorry guys...
